TLDR: Observations carried out during 1999--2003 in a commercial vineyard in northeastern Italy showed that densities of T. caudatus were often correlated to downy mildew spread on the vegetation, and tydeid densities were often positively correlated to the extent of leaf surface showing symptoms.},
