  abstract = {The objective of the study was to conduct an extensive energy and microclimatic assessment of different greenhouse covering materials. Single glass (CL) and three types of double polyethylene (PE) claddings were compared. The double polyethylene cladding consisting of an anti-fog thermal film for the inner layer and a standard PE film for the outer layer was the most energy efficient. It had an average measured heat transfer coefficient (U value) of 2.9 W me2 K- `. The average U value for the other PE cladding was 3.4 W m {\textasciitilde}' K- '. The use of thermal screens in the PE houses during the night reduced heat loss rates by 23-24\%.},
